        " permutation."}], "Usage", CellID -> 294531438, 
      ExpressionUUID -> "1c5e0f27-f869-41ba-b406-22a9b66faa74"], 
     Cell["Returns a canonical contraction path \[LongDash] a list of pairs \
{{i, j}, \[Ellipsis]} where each step removes the tensors at positions i and \
j from the working list and appends their pairwise contraction (the \
opt_einsum convention).", "Notes", CellID -> 238694475, 
      ExpressionUUID -> "2cb65633-6e27-46c0-b12e-81b437c1e20f"], 
     Cell[TextData[{"The path is optimal under the chosen ", 
        Cell[BoxData[ButtonBox["Method", BaseStyle -> "Link", 
           ButtonData -> "paclet:ref/Method"]], "InlineFormula", 
         ExpressionUUID -> "74bc615f-2ec5-47b4-81e5-52eb642430f5"], ". Search \
uses dynamic programming and is exponential in the number of tensors in the \
worst case; use ", Cell[BoxData[ButtonBox["GreedyContractionPath", 
           BaseStyle -> "Link", ButtonData -> 
            "paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/GreedyContractionPath"]], 
         "InlineFormula", ExpressionUUID -> 
          "bad5bc43-4a0f-4b61-b844-aaabf064eab8"], 
        " for networks where exhaustive search is impractical."}], "Notes", 
      CellID -> 453970307, ExpressionUUID -> 
       "72f68cad-4c8e-4f10-9cda-892e887793b0"], 
     Cell[TextData[{"The default ", 
        Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{ButtonBox["Method", BaseStyle -> "Link", 
             ButtonData -> "paclet:ref/Method"], "\[Rule]", 
            StyleBox["\"size\"", ShowStringCharacters -> True]}]], 
         "InlineFormula", ExpressionUUID -> 
          "aa771385-ec52-4152-a538-8f01f9d4c745"], " minimizes the size of \
the largest intermediate tensor produced during contraction."}], "Notes", 
      CellID -> 693361215, ExpressionUUID -> 
       "2a77e26f-7089-4432-97f6-4182d721038c"], 
     Cell[TextData[{"When the input has a hyper-edge (an index that appears \
in three or more tensors), ", Cell[BoxData[ButtonBox[
           "OptimalContractionPath", BaseStyle -> "Link", 
           ButtonData -> 
            "paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/OptimalContractionPath"]], 
         "InlineFormula", ExpressionUUID -> 
          "595fc836-b7d2-41c0-aaf9-891360bd51a5"], " first applies ", 
        Cell[BoxData[ButtonBox["BinaryTensorNetwork", BaseStyle -> "Link", 
           ButtonData -> 
            "paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/BinaryTensorNetwork"]], 
         "InlineFormula", ExpressionUUID -> 
          "e6ef11f3-3b26-4c78-8978-0a3eec21b88a"], " to insert copy tensors \
and reduce the network to pairwise edges before searching."}], "Notes", 
      CellID -> 601743941, ExpressionUUID -> 
       "9fcf7c43-ef3c-4aa3-87c2-49a870e4ae11"], 
     Cell[TextData[
       {"The search backend is a Rust library function loaded from the ", 
        Cell[BoxData[ButtonBox[RowBox[{"Wolfram", "/", "PacletExtensions"}], 
           BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", ButtonData -> 
            {URL[
              "https://www.wolframcloud.com/obj/nikm/PacletExtensions.paclet"]\
, None}]], "InlineFormula", ExpressionUUID -> 
          "a2b7ae81-a70d-4b85-b23c-c9db1f8afda5"], 
        " paclet; the library function is called ", 
        Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["optimize_optimal", ShowStringCharacters -> 
            False]], "InlineFormula", ExpressionUUID -> 
          "ffe2bc3f-c502-4bc2-9233-cb8c4a7e53f8"], "."}], "Notes", 
      CellID -> 11650920, ExpressionUUID -> 
